# The RAM tiers are symlinks out of the repository. Nothing in them is ever
# committed; they hold logs, builds, and scratch that is regenerated on demand.
tmp

# Deprecated temporary scripts are kept for exactly one commit and then removed,
# so they are never ignored -- they are supposed to show up in the record once.

# Editor and OS litter.
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# The browsable documentation is a **view**, not a source. Every page under docs/HTML
# is written by ./build-documentation from the Markdown that sits beside it -- checked,
# not assumed: a build touches all 165 of them and leaves nothing behind but the
# placeholder that keeps the directory in the repository at all.
#
# Committing generated pages means every prose edit arrives as a diff of itself plus a
# hundred and sixty files of machine output, and it means two people who both ran the
# build have a conflict in something neither of them wrote.
#
# Run ./build-documentation to get them back. Nothing is lost by their absence.
docs/HTML/*
!docs/HTML/.gitkeep
